<SizeGuide
  title="Uniqlo Size Guide — Does Uniqlo Run Small? (Charts & Tips) | Attirel"
  description="Uniqlo runs small with a slim Japanese cut — most Western shoppers size up one. Full Uniqlo size charts with US/UK/EU conversions and fitting tips."
  brand="Uniqlo"
  verdictQuestion="Does Uniqlo run small?"
  charts={charts}
>
  <Fragment slot="verdict">
    <strong>Yes — Uniqlo runs small for most Western shoppers.</strong> Uniqlo cuts to a slim
    Japanese fit block: narrower through the shoulders and chest, with shorter sleeves and
    torsos. If you're between sizes — or buying outerwear or knits you'll layer — size up one.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="tips">
    <li><strong>Regional stock differs:</strong> items from Uniqlo's US/EU ranges are adjusted upward, but Japan-spec items (and anything bought abroad) run a full size smaller.</li>
    <li><strong>Sleeves and torso run short</strong> — if you have long arms or a long torso, size up even when the width fits.</li>
    <li><strong>Heattech and Airism</strong> are meant to fit snug against the skin — stay true to size for the base-layer effect.</li>
    <li><strong>Supima cotton tees</strong> can shrink slightly in a hot wash — wash cold or size up.</li>
    <li><strong>U line and collabs</strong> (Uniqlo U, JW Anderson) cut boxier and oversized — check the model measurements; many shoppers size down.</li>
  </Fragment>
</SizeGuide>
